[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, ensuring that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m We will consider the different possible scenarios for the subcommittee:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 1. 1 Republican and 4 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 2. 2 Republicans and 3 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 3. 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 4. 4 Republicans and 1 Democrat
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Let's calculate the number of ways for each scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m ### 1. 1 Republican and 4 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 1 Republican: $\binom{8}{1}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 4 Democrats: $\binom{6}{4}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Total ways for this scenario: $\binom{8}{1} \times \binom{6}{4}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m ### 2. 2 Republicans and 3 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 2 Republicans: $\binom{8}{2}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 3 Democrats: $\binom{6}{3}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Total ways for this scenario: $\binom{8}{2} \times \binom{6}{3}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m ### 3. 3 Republicans and 2 Democrats
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 3 Republicans: $\binom{8}{3}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 2 Democrats: $\binom{6}{2}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Total ways for this scenario: $\binom{8}{3} \times \binom{6}{2}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m ### 4. 4 Republicans and 1 Democrat
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 4 Republicans: $\binom{8}{4}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Choose 1 Democrat: $\binom{6}{1}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m - Total ways for this scenario: $\binom{8}{4} \times \binom{6}{1}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Finally, we sum up the number of ways from all scenarios and wrap the final answer within $\boxed{}$.
