[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To find the value of \( x \) given that the arithmetic mean of 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is 9, we start with the formula for the arithmetic mean of a set of numbers. The arithmetic mean is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Given the numbers 7, 2, \( x \), and 10, the arithmetic mean is calculated as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \text{Arithmetic mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m We know that the arithmetic mean is 9, so we can set up the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 9 = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, simplify the numerator on the right side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 7 + 2 + 10 = 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
