[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To find the value of \( x \) such that the arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is 9, we start by using the formula for the arithmetic mean of a set of numbers. The arithmetic mean of a set of \( n \) numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by \( n \). In this case, we have 4 numbers, so the arithmetic mean is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
