[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To solve the problem of forming a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the requirement that the subcommittee includes at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. This involves calculating the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and then subtracting the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is not in compliance with the given condition (i.e., it contains no Republicans or no Democrats).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
