[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To find the value of \( x \), we start by using the definition of the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. Here, the set of numbers is \( 7, 2, x, 10 \) and the mean is 9. Therefore, we can write the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, we simplify the numerator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 7 + 2 + 10 + x = 19 + x
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Next, we eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To isolate \( x \), we subtract 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Therefore, the value of \( x \) is \(\boxed{17}\).
