[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 91 + 53 > 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 144 > 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m This is also false. For \( x = 21 \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 7(21) + 53 > 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 147 + 53 > 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 200 > 200 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m This is true, but we need to check if it satisfies the modulo condition:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 7(21) + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 147 + 53 \equiv 0 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 100 \equiv 4 \pmod{8} \]
