[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 8n \equiv -29 + 32 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 8n \equiv 3 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Since \( 8n \) is always a multiple of 8, we need to find the remainder when 53 is divided by 8, which is 5. So we rewrite it as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 5 \equiv 5 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Thus, we need:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 5 \equiv -3n \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ -3n \equiv -5 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ 3n \equiv 5 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To solve for \( n \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 3 modulo 8. The inverse \( x \) satisfies \( 3x \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \). Checking values, we find that \( x = 3 \) works because \( 3 \cdot 3 = 9 \equiv 1 \pmod{8} \). So we multiply both sides of the congruence \( 3n \equiv 5 \pmod{8} \) by 3:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ n \equiv 15 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[ n \equiv 7 \pmod{8} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m So the smallest positive \( n \) is 7. The total number of coins before finding the bag of 53 coins is \( 7 \cdot 7 + 53 = 49 + 53 = 102 \).
