[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with the condition that the subcommittee must have at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting and combinations.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 available members without any restrictions. This can be calculated using the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) elements from a set of \( n \) elements without regard to the order of selection.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members from 14 members is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
