[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats such that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. This means we first calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and then subtract the number of subcommittees that are not balanced (i.e., all members are Republicans or all members are Democrats).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 members (8 Republicans + 6 Democrats):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Next, calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is entirely composed of Republicans:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Then, calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is entirely composed of Democrats:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m The number of subcommittees that are not balanced (i.e., all Republican or all Democratic) is the sum of the above two results:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Therefore, the number of subcommittees that have at least one member from each party is the total number of subcommittees minus the number of subcommittees that are not balanced:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
