[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats, with at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting. This means we will first calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 people, and then subtract the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from 14 people:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5!9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 2. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Republicans. Since we have 8 Republicans, the number of ways to choose 5 Republicans from 8 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5!3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 3. Calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is all Democrats. Since we have 6 Democrats, the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats from 6 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5!1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 4. Subtract the number of all-Republican and all-Democratic subcommittees from the total number of subcommittees to get the number of subcommittees with at least one member from each party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 2002 - \binom{8}{5} - \binom{6}{5} = 2002 - 56 - 6 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
