[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from a Senate committee consisting of 8 Republicans and 6 Democrats such that the subcommittee has at least one member from each party, we can use the principle of complementary counting.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members from the 14 members of the committee. This is given by the combination formula \( \binom{n}{k} \), which represents the number of ways to choose \( k \) items from \( n \) items without regard to the order of selection.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m The total number of ways to choose 5 members out of 14 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Next, we calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that is entirely Republican or entirely Democrat. The number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m The number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that is either entirely Republican or entirely Democrat is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m The number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members minus the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is entirely Republican or entirely Democrat:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} - \left( \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} \right) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Thus, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \boxed{1940}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
