[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To determine the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party (Republicans and Democrats), we can use the principle of complementary counting. Specifically, we will calculate the total number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members and subtract the number of ways to form a subcommittee that is either all Republicans or all Democrats.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, we calculate the total number of ways to choose 5 members out of the 14 available members (8 Republicans and 6 Democrats). This is given by the combination formula \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} = \frac{14!}{5!(14-5)!} = \frac{14!}{5! \cdot 9!} = 2002
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Next, we calculate the number of ways to form a subcommittee that consists entirely of Republicans or entirely of Democrats. The number of ways to choose 5 Republicans out of 8 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} = \frac{8!}{5!(8-5)!} = \frac{8!}{5! \cdot 3!} = 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m And the number of ways to choose 5 Democrats out of 6 is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{6}{5} = \frac{6!}{5!(6-5)!} = \frac{6!}{5! \cdot 1!} = 6
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m So the total number of ways to form a subcommittee that has either all Republicans or all Democrats is the sum of the above two combinations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5} = 56 + 6 = 62
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Finally, we use complementary counting to find the number of ways to form a subcommittee that has at least one member from each party:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \binom{14}{5} - \left(\binom{8}{5} + \binom{6}{5}\right) = 2002 - 62 = 1940
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Therefore, the number of ways to form a subcommittee of 5 members that has at least one member from each party is \(\boxed{1940}\).
