[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m To find the value of \( x \), we need to use the definition of the arithmetic mean. The arithmetic mean of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the count of the numbers. Here, the arithmetic mean of the numbers 7, 2, \( x \), and 10 is given as 9. We can set up the following equation based on this definition:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \text{Arithmetic mean} = \frac{7 + 2 + x + 10}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m First, simplify the numerator on the left side of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \frac{19 + x}{4} = 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Next, eliminate the fraction by multiplying both sides of the equation by 4:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 19 + x = 36
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Then, isolate \( x \) by subtracting 19 from both sides of the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m x = 36 - 19
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m x = 17
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2971282)[0m Thus, the value of \( x \) is \(\boxed{17}\).
